Z||000000||2M4 Dale||05-21-2000||09:08 PM||||Well my 5 spd. worked fine yesterday...Today it seems as though I've lost 5th gear and reverse. How can I tell if this is a shifter problem or a Isuzu problem ? 1st through 4th gears work just fine. Any ideas.........||||reg||8
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||05-21-2000||11:40 PM||||Help me out here guys.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||05-21-2000||11:59 PM||||Gate cable?  Happened to me twice, but I only had first and second gears.<BR>Put it in neutral and see if the gate selector moves as you move the shifter side to side.<BR>If you've already checked this, I'm out of ideas.<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 05-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||05-23-2000||07:01 AM||||Thanks 2birds, I still havn't gotten around to working on my problem. Probably tommorrow I'll check it all out. I've read and reread the Haynes service book on adjustment procedures. I'll try that stuff first. I just hope that I don't have a tranny problem!||||reg||1
Z||000004||2M4 Dale||05-23-2000||11:53 PM||||OK...There are two cables to the tranny. One is the shifter cable and the other is the selector cable. My shifter cable was/is working OK. The selector cable would not throw into the third gate...the one with fifth and reverse. Tonight I had a friend look at this thing with me and we determined that the plunger/selector fork wasn't going in far enough to reach the third gate. So we took a block of wood and while I worked the shifter my buddy tapped on the plunger. IT WORKED. The plunger was on a bind. After we got it into position the first time we had to do it again but now the doggone thing thing works fine. I'm gonna hose the whole works down with lube tommorrow and hopefully I won't have any more trouble.<P>Has any one else had this problem ???||||reg||6
Z||000005||2birds||05-24-2000||08:03 PM||||The gate cable pulls to go into 5th and reverse, if I remember correctly, and the easy thing to do is undo it at the transaxle, since it's not an adjustable point.  Then pull on the cable end to see if it moves the shifter handle.  Piece of cake.  Best of luck.||||reg||1
